# Commit message style

- Main description: under 200 characters, imperative mood ("add", "fix", "remove", "update")
- Never use the words "refactor" or "enhance" — say specifically what changed instead
- If multiple distinct things changed, use a short subject line then bullet points
- No filler: skip "this commit", "in order to", "various improvements"
- One bullet per distinct change — drop it if everything fits on one line

## Examples

Good (single change):
```
fix nav links disappearing on mobile at 768px breakpoint
```

Good (multiple changes):
```
update tourist page hero section

- swap placeholder copy for final directions text
- remove unused EventCard import
- fix broken link to /cats
```

Bad:
```
Refactor and enhance the layout components to improve performance and user experience across multiple pages with various updates
```
